headless = f'''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="crumbs"><a href="index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Headless</span></div><span class="eyebrow">TYPO3 beyond templates</span><h1>Content freedom.<br><em>Engineering clarity.</em></h1><p>Headless project patterns for teams pairing TYPO3 content with a separate frontend. Designed around explicit contracts, editor needs and maintainable delivery.</p>{btn('Talk about a headless project','contact.html')}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><div><span class="eyebrow">A considered approach</span><h2>Start with the content model.</h2><p class="lead lead-mt-20">A good headless build begins with what editors need to create and what the frontend needs to render. The API is the bridge, not the whole strategy.</p></div><div class="statement-list"><div class="statement"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>Content contract</h3><p>Define types, fields and naming before components multiply.</p></div></div><div class="statement"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Frontend freedom</h3><p>Plan React or Next.js rendering around actual content needs.</p></div></div><div class="statement"><span class="index">03</span><div><h3>Editor experience</h3><p>Keep preview, relationships and publishing understandable.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="section-sm dark-section"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Reference architecture</span><h2>Separate concerns.<br>Keep the connection legible.</h2><div class="proof-grid proof-grid-mt-35"><div class="proof-panel"><span class="badge dark">01 / TYPO3</span><h3 class="proof-panel-title-sm">Structured content</h3><p>Editorial models and workflows that reflect the organization.</p></div><div class="proof-panel"><span class="badge dark">02 / Frontend</span><h3 class="proof-panel-title-sm">Purpose-built experience</h3><p>A frontend shaped to the site, app or channel it serves.</p></div></div></div></section>'''
