docs = f'''<section class="page-hero compact"><div class="container"><div class="crumbs"><a href="index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Docs</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Documentation concept</span><h1>Start with clarity.</h1><p>An example of how CMSMotive product documentation can make installation, structure and customization easy to follow. Commands and paths below are illustrative until packages are released.</p></div></section><div class="container docs-layout"><aside class="docs-side" aria-label="Documentation sections"><div class="footer-label">On this page</div><a class="active" href="#getting-started">Getting started</a><a href="#requirements">Requirements</a><a href="#installation">Installation</a><a href="#structure">Theme structure</a><a href="#accessibility-docs">Accessibility</a><a href="#support">Support</a></aside><article class="docs-content"><h2 id="getting-started">Getting started</h2><p>CMSMotive documentation is planned around the questions a team has when a package joins an existing TYPO3 project: what it needs, how to install it and what can safely be changed.</p><p class="notice">This is a documentation design preview. Do not run the example package command until a verified release is published.</p><h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2><p>Each released product will publish its tested TYPO3 version range, PHP requirements, dependencies and browser support in one place. No support matrix is claimed by this concept page.</p><h2 id="installation">Installation example</h2><p>A Composer-first path keeps installation visible in the project dependency graph.</p><div class="docs-code"><div class="code-head"><span>terminal / illustrative</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="composer require cmsmotive/theme-nordform">Copy command</button></div><pre class="code"><span class="blue">$</span> composer require <b>cmsmotive/theme-nordform</b></pre></div><p>After release, the product docs would cover site set configuration, content setup, asset building and deployment checks step by step.</p><h2 id="structure">Theme structure</h2><p>The intended structure separates TYPO3 configuration, Fluid templates, assets and documentation so custom work remains easy to locate.</p><div class="docs-code"><div class="code-head"><span>example / package layout</span></div><pre class="code">Configuration/\n  ContentBlocks/\n  TypoScript/\nResources/Private/\n  Layouts/\n  Partials/\n  Templates/\nDocumentation/</pre></div><h2 id="accessibility-docs">Accessibility</h2><p>Product documentation should explain keyboard behavior, supported content patterns and known limitations. A release audit report belongs beside those notes, with a date and tested version.</p><h2 id="support">Support and change history</h2><p>Released packages should include a changelog, migration notes and a clear support route. For the concept, send project questions to <a href="mailto:hello@cmsmotive.com" class="text-link">hello@cmsmotive.com</a>.</p></article><aside class="docs-toc" aria-label="Related links"><div class="footer-label">Explore next</div><a href="theme-nordform.html">Nordform preview</a><a href="blog-composer.html">Composer workflow</a><a href="contact.html">Ask a question</a></aside></div><div class="docs-spacer"></div>'''
page("docs.html", "Documentation", "Explore the planned CMSMotive documentation structure for TYPO3 themes and products.", docs, "docs.html")

